---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---

<Marketing
	title="Features · Obzly"
	description="Logs, traces, metrics, dashboards, alerts, MCP and enterprise features in the open source Obzly image."
	current="features"
>
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="page-hero">
				<div class="eyebrow">Features</div>
				<h1>What Obzly does</h1>
				<p class="lede">Every feature on this page is in the open source image. Nothing here needs a licence key.</p>
				<nav class="jump" aria-label="Feature sections">
					<a href="#logs">Logs</a><a href="#traces">Traces</a><a href="#metrics">Metrics</a>
					<a href="#dashboards">Dashboards &amp; Alerts</a><a href="#ai">AI observability &amp; MCP</a><a href="#enterprise">Enterprise</a>
				</nav>
			</div>

			<article class="feat" id="logs">
				<div class="txt">
					<div class="eyebrow">Logs</div>
					<h2>Search a week of logs in seconds</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><b>Search</b> by text and field, with a query builder or SQL and a field sidebar.</li>
						<li><b>Live tail</b> with cursor paging, so new arrivals don't shift the page you're reading.</li>
						<li><b>Patterns and anomalies</b>: new, spiking and dropping patterns against an earlier period.</li>
						<li><b>Log context</b>: the logs before and after any result, from the same pod or service.</li>
						<li><b>Promoted fields</b>: up to 12 per project become typed columns for fast filters and number ranges.</li>
						<li><b>Wide searches</b> read newest-first and stop once the page is full. Searching for an ID skips every segment whose bloom filter lacks it.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="specimen">
					<div class="lbl">Search bar</div>
					<pre><span class="k">level</span>:error <span class="k">service_name</span>:api <span class="s">"timeout"</span></pre>
					<div class="lbl">Attribute names are PromQL-safe</div>
					<pre><span class="c">resource.k8s.pod.name</span>  →  <span class="k">k8s_pod_name</span>
	<span class="c">system.cpu.time</span>        →  <span class="k">system_cpu_time</span></pre>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="feat" id="traces">
				<div class="txt">
					<div class="eyebrow">Traces</div>
					<h2>Follow a request across services</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><b>OTLP traces</b> over gRPC or HTTP, from any OpenTelemetry SDK.</li>
						<li><b>Trace explorer</b> and a <b>service map</b> built from real calls.</li>
						<li><b>Jaeger-compatible query API</b>: existing Jaeger clients work unmodified.</li>
						<li><b>Tail sampling</b> keeps whole traces, not random spans.</li>
						<li><b>Zero-code traces</b> on Kubernetes with OpenTelemetry eBPF Instrumentation (OBI).</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="specimen">
					<div class="lbl">Trace · POST /checkout · 412 ms</div>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-label="Example trace waterfall with five spans">
						<g class="d-s"><text x="0" y="16">frontend</text><text x="0" y="44">checkout</text><text x="0" y="72">payments</text><text x="0" y="100">postgres</text><text x="0" y="128">kafka</text></g>
						<rect x="90" y="6" width="320" height="14" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)"/>
						<rect x="110" y="34" width="270" height="14" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)" opacity="0.75"/>
						<rect x="140" y="62" width="190" height="14" rx="3" fill="var(--amber)"/>
						<rect x="150" y="90" width="60" height="14" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)" opacity="0.5"/>
						<rect x="340" y="118" width="34" height="14" rx="3" fill="var(--accent)" opacity="0.5"/>
						<text class="d-a" x="336" y="73" style="fill:var(--amber)">slow</text>
					</svg>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="feat" id="metrics">
				<div class="txt">
					<div class="eyebrow">Metrics</div>
					<h2>Keep Grafana, drop the metrics stack</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><b>OTLP and Prometheus remote-write</b> ingestion.</li>
						<li><b>PromQL-compatible API</b>: point an existing Grafana Prometheus datasource at Obzly.</li>
						<li><b>Rollups</b> at 5 minutes and 1 hour keep long ranges fast and can outlive raw samples.</li>
						<li><b>Host and Kubernetes metrics</b> from the generated Collector config.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="specimen">
					<div class="lbl">PromQL, no quoting needed</div>
					<pre><span class="k">sum by</span> (k8s_pod_name) (system_cpu_time)</pre>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 420 110" role="img" aria-label="Example metric line chart">
						<g stroke="var(--line)" stroke-width="1"><line x1="0" y1="20" x2="420" y2="20"/><line x1="0" y1="55" x2="420" y2="55"/><line x1="0" y1="90" x2="420" y2="90"/></g>
						<polyline points="0,80 40,70 80,74 120,52 160,58 200,40 240,46 280,28 320,34 360,22 400,30 420,26" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2.5"/>
						<polyline points="0,92 40,88 80,90 120,82 160,84 200,76 240,80 280,70 320,74 360,66 400,70 420,68" fill="none" stroke="var(--amber)" stroke-width="2"/>
					</svg>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="feat" id="dashboards">
				<div class="txt">
					<div class="eyebrow">Dashboards &amp; Alerts</div>
					<h2>Bring your dashboards, get paged quickly</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><b>Dashboards</b>: build your own, or import Grafana or OpenObserve dashboard JSON.</li>
						<li><b>Alert rules</b> over metrics (PromQL), logs (counts of a search, optionally per field) or traces (count, errors, latency percentiles).</li>
						<li><b>for durations, repeat intervals, labels</b> and a live preview.</li>
						<li><b>Notifications</b> to webhooks, Slack, PagerDuty or email, through an outbox with retries and silences. About 15 seconds from rule to notification.</li>
						<li><b>Incidents</b> group error logs, failed spans and their shared traces.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="specimen">
					<div class="lbl">Example rule</div>
					<pre><span class="c"># Logs: count of a search</span>
	search:  <span class="s">level:error service_name:checkout</span>
	when:    count &gt; 50
	for:     5m
	notify:  Slack, PagerDuty</pre>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="feat" id="ai">
				<div class="txt">
					<div class="eyebrow">AI observability &amp; MCP</div>
					<h2>Let your assistant read production</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><b>MCP server at /mcp</b>: Claude Code, Cursor, claude.ai and Claude Desktop can search logs, run SQL over them, inspect traces and service maps, and run PromQL.</li>
						<li><b>Read-only</b>, with exactly the access your account has. Tokens work only on <code>/mcp</code>.</li>
						<li><b>Browser sign-in</b> for claude.ai and Claude Desktop, with connected apps listed and revocable in your profile.</li>
						<li><b>Multi-site aware</b>: one endpoint covers every Site you can access.</li>
						<li><b>Claude Code usage</b> per project: cost, tokens, cache use and sessions.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="specimen">
					<div class="lbl">Claude Code</div>
					<pre>claude mcp add --transport http obzly \
		https://obzly.example.com/mcp \
		--header <span class="s">"Authorization: Bearer obz_pat_..."</span></pre>
				</div>
			</article>

			<article class="feat" id="enterprise">
				<div class="txt">
					<div class="eyebrow">Enterprise</div>
					<h2>Identity, scale and recovery</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><b>SSO</b> through any OIDC provider, with Microsoft Entra ID group mapping.</li>
						<li><b>SCIM 2.0</b> from Okta or Entra ID; <b>TOTP MFA</b> required for admins.</li>
						<li><b>Organizations, teams and plans</b> with per-organization quotas.</li>
						<li><b>High availability</b>: rolling updates with readiness draining, leases so each shard has one owner, no single query node.</li>
						<li><b>Durable ingest</b>: losing an api pod, a worker or one broker loses no acknowledged data.</li>
						<li><b>Disaster recovery</b> runbooks with a measured restore drill (RPO under a minute) and a weekly integrity audit.</li>
						<li><b>Audit log</b> of every change and every denied request.</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<div class="specimen">
					<div class="lbl">When the buffer is full</div>
					<pre>HTTP 429  /  gRPC RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED
	<span class="c"># OTel Collectors retry; nothing acknowledged is lost</span></pre>
					<div class="lbl">Query guardrail</div>
					<pre>QUERY_MAX_SCAN_GB=<span class="s">100</span>  <span class="c"># refuse runaway queries before reading</span></pre>
				</div>
			</article>
		</div>
</Marketing>
